<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply off $2.1 bln in Sept 16 wk.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply off $2.1 bln in Sept 16 wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply fell $2.1 billion in the September 16 week to $3,771.0 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure rose $11.9 billion to $4,775.9 billion. M-1 fell $4.7 billion to $1,091.8 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,764.3 billion versus $3,760.1 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
